{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/712402-creating-chars-above-cliath","id":712402,"title":"Creating chars above Cliath?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-21T07:56:27-07:00","id":712402,"title":"Creating chars above Cliath?","content":"wheres the rules in W20 for advanced charachters? am running a game on rpol so its relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T09:40:52-07:00","id":712592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/712402-creating-chars-above-cliath#post712402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wheres the rules in W20 for advanced charachters? am running a game on rpol so its relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably nowhere. What questions do you have? Are you looking for suggestions for XP ranges for Fostern, Adren, Athro, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T09:44:05-07:00","id":712605,"title":"","content":"W20 Rage Across the World, page 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T07:21:59-07:00","id":714440,"title":"","content":"A question just got asked, how to handle rites for advanced chars, since backgrounds only go to 5<br /> <br /> Ideas?<br /> <br /> other issue is Talens and Fetishes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T08:29:23-07:00","id":714613,"title":"","content":"If I have a character who for whatever reason wants more than one fetish I require them to spend the points multiple times. Example: Trevor is playing a Shadow Lord Ahroun. He is joining the pack as a replacement. He wants a fetish weapon in this case a spear he wants a butterfly spirit bound to the fetish so that it can change sizes. I agree and after considering it state that it will be a level 3 fetish. Trevor also would like a fetish that will help with healing himself or others he suggests a cloth and proposes a bear spirit. Again I agree and assign it a level 3. Two fetishes equaling 6 points.<br /> I would never allow a player to start with a level 6 fetish, those should be restricted to NPCS or the main storyline of a chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T09:11:42-07:00","id":714676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/712402-creating-chars-above-cliath?p=714440#post714440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question just got asked, how to handle rites for advanced chars, since backgrounds only go to 5<br /> <br /> Ideas?<br /> <br /> other issue is Talens and Fetishes...</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, the Rites background seems rather expensive to me. Consider the basic equipment of a Theurge:<br /> Rite of Summoning - because Theurges who can't summon spirits do not get taken seriously by me<br /> Rite of Contrition - because there's always someone in the pack who will fuck up and upset the spirits<br /> Rite of Talisman Dedication - because I really like not having to buy new clothes after every change<br /> Rite of Cleansing - because you don't want your pack to switch sides after the first few missions<br /> <br /> And suddenly, the Theurge has spent a number of background points that would alternatively make them a millionaire or the scion of one of the greatest Garou lines to ever live.<br /> Thus, I'd suggest handing out a few free points. For a Theurge at late-Fostern, I handed out 13 free points, for a less ritually inclined auspice, I'd go for perhaps 5 or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:00:34-07:00","id":714715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/712402-creating-chars-above-cliath?p=714676#post714676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In general, the Rites background seems rather expensive to me. Consider the basic equipment of a Theurge:<br /> Rite of Summoning - because Theurges who can't summon spirits do not get taken seriously by me<br /> Rite of Contrition - because there's always someone in the pack who will fuck up and upset the spirits<br /> Rite of Talisman Dedication - because I really like not having to buy new clothes after every change<br /> Rite of Cleansing - because you don't want your pack to switch sides after the first few missions</div> </div> </div> </div>I always considered Rite of Contrition to be a Ragabash or Philodox rite. <br /> I agree Summoning and Cleansing usually end up on my Theurges.<br /> Rite of Talisman Dedication doesn't have to be Theurge specific, so long as <i>someone</i> in the pack has it.<br /> <br /> That being said, for characters starting at higher ranks, I usually use a multiplier to their points invested into rites or fetishes. Doing those backgrounds that way worked out well in games I've ran. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:41:19-07:00","id":714771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/712402-creating-chars-above-cliath?p=714440#post714440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question just got asked, how to handle rites for advanced chars, since backgrounds only go to 5<br /> <br /> Ideas?<br /> <br /> other issue is Talens and Fetishes...</div> </div> </div> </div>Something alone the line of costing for the Totem Background might clear that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T08:32:45-07:00","id":734837,"title":"","content":"No need to change the Fetish background. Fetish are still items of rare power; the book gives the option for starting characters of takign a fetish up to level 5 - but that's because player characters tend to be the exception and even then it should require a background explanation. They are not D&amp;D magic items and higher Rank character shouldn't simply hoard them.<br /> In lieu of that you could consider giving out free talens to more advanced characters. Those are noted as being sort of werewolf currency, to be hoarded or traded fro favors. An advanced PC probably has a nice cache of talens available, especially if anyone in the pack knows the Rite of Binding.<br /> Rites however are a little different. They can be learned in story without an expenditure of experience points, they only require narration. Since for advanced characters background takes the place of that I'd suggest doing away with Rites and giving a character whatever rites it seems logical they could have learned based on background, with special care and a deeper explanation needed for rites that could be deemed too powerful or out of place (ie Gaia's Vengeful Teeth, Rite of Caern Building, a non-Theurge trying to start with a buttload of Mystic Rites, camps' secret rites; in contrast probably any Fostern had the chance to be thaught the Rite of Talisman Dedication andthe Rite of Contrition if he bothered to ask)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}